1
00:05:38,823 --> 00:05:44,823
How did one woman save 2500 children?

2
00:11:17,647 --> 00:11:23,647
The Courageous Heart of Irena Sendler is a drama, war
film directed by John Kent Harrison.

3
00:16:56,470 --> 00:17:02,470
Irena Sendler is a Catholic social worker who has sympathized with the Jews since her childhood, when
her physician father died of typhus contracted while treating poor Jewish patients.

4
00:22:35,294 --> 00:22:41,294
When she initially proposes saving Jewish children from the Warsaw Ghetto, her idea is met with
skepticism by fellow workers, her parish priest, and even her own mother Janina.

5
00:28:14,117 --> 00:28:20,117
Irena Sendler, played by Anna Paquin.

6
00:33:52,941 --> 00:33:58,941
Stefan Zgrzembski, played by Goran Višnjić.

7
00:39:31,764 --> 00:39:37,764
Ewa Rozenfeld, played by Michelle Dockery.

8
00:45:10,588 --> 00:45:16,588
Hannah Rozenfeld, played by Danuta Stenka.

9
00:50:49,411 --> 00:50:55,411
Jadwiga, played by Maja Ostaszewska.

10
00:56:28,235 --> 00:56:34,235
Dr. Janusz Korczak, played by Krzysztof Pieczyński.

11
01:02:07,058 --> 01:02:13,058
The Courageous Heart of Irena Sendler is a 2009
television film directed by John Kent Harrison.

12
01:07:45,882 --> 01:07:51,882
The teleplay by Harrison and Lawrence John Spagnola, based on the 2007 biography Die Mutter der Holocaust-Kinder: Irena Sendler und die geretteten Kinder aus dem
Warschauer Ghetto, focuses on Irena Sendler, a Polish social worker who smuggled approximately 2,500 Jewish children to safety during World War II.

13
01:13:24,705 --> 01:13:30,705
The Hallmark Hall of Fame production was filmed on location in Riga, Latvia.

14
01:19:03,529 --> 01:19:09,529
It was broadcast on CBS channels in North America on April 19, 2009, and
released to DVD in Hallmark Gold Crown stores in June of that year.

15
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
The film explores themes of nazi, holocaust (shoah), world
war ii, biography, based on true story.

16
01:30:21,176 --> 01:30:27,176
The tone is emotional.
